---
const principles = [
  {
    title: 'No accounts',
    body: 'There is no sign-up, no login, no session management. Board access is granted by the URL fragment. Lose the token, look it up in the JSON file.',
  },
  {
    title: 'No cloud dependency',
    body: 'The server stores board state as JSON files on disk. No managed database, no external API, no service that can disappear or change its pricing.',
  },
  {
    title: 'No telemetry',
    body: 'The app makes no outbound network calls. Nothing phones home. Nothing is measured externally. Your board activity stays on your hardware.',
  },
  {
    title: 'No version lock-in',
    body: 'Board files are plain JSON with a documented structure. You can read them, back them up, and migrate them without any special tooling.',
  },
];
---
<section class="border-t border-rule bg-sage-50 px-6 py-20 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-sage-700 opacity-60">Operating model</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Explicit about what it <em class="italic text-sage-600">doesn't</em> do.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The simplest way to build trust with self-hosters is to keep the scope narrow and make the operating model legible. FridgeShare does this by staying out of infrastructure it doesn't need.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-px bg-rule sm:grid-cols-2">
      {principles.map((item) => (
        <div class="bg-sage-50 p-8 hover:bg-white transition-colors group">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-sage-700 transition-colors">
            {item.title}
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{item.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-px bg-rule">
      <div class="bg-sage-50 px-8 py-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">
          For public deployments: set
          <code class="mx-1 rounded bg-white px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-ink border border-rule">SELFHOST_ADMIN_TOKEN</code>
          and back up the
          <code class="mx-1 rounded bg-white px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-ink border border-rule">data/</code>
          directory. Everything else is optional configuration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
